{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuilds"},"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HeadwireMacKit"}],"title":"The App Store and Direct builds","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"abstract":[{"text":"How one helper source tree becomes two binaries, and how each feature finds out whether it can run.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/helperbuilds"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Headwire Helper ships in two builds from the same code:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The App Store build"}]},{"text":" is sandboxed and compiles no private API. It is the default: a plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" makes it.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Direct build"}]},{"text":" is signed with Developer ID, notarized and unsandboxed. It adds the code compiled under ","type":"text"},{"code":"HEADWIRE_PRIVATE_API","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the virtual display that extends the Mac onto the device, Apple’s Sidecar started from the menu, and answering the Mac’s side of Bluetooth pairing without a system dialog. Each of these is checked at run time and turns off rather than crashes when macOS has changed it.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Helper input is compiled under a second switch, ","type":"text"},{"code":"HEADWIRE_HELPER_INPUT","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is on by default in both builds. A build without it keeps streaming and shows input as unavailable.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This documentation is generated from the App Store build, so the Direct build’s private-API types do not appear in it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Which build is running","level":3,"anchor":"Which-build-is-running","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/current","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" reads the two compile-time switches and reports the build’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/Distribution-swift.enum","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and whether helper input is compiled in. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperBuild\/launchLine(version:dryRun:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is the first line the helper logs at launch.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Whether a feature runs","level":3,"anchor":"Whether-a-feature-runs","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperFeatures\/resolve(_:grants:build:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" combines three inputs into one ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for each feature:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The menu’s switch for it, in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/HelperToggles","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Every switch starts off: the helper is optional, and streaming, input and extending the Mac begin only when the person turns them on.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What macOS has granted, in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/PermissionGrants","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". A switch that is on without its permission is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/needs(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Onboarding","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" walks the person through that one permission.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What the build contains. A feature the build lacks is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/unavailable(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" with an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" whose ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/Unavailability\/menuText","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is shown on the greyed-out control.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The extended display also needs streaming, so with its switch on and streaming not running it is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HeadwireMacKit\/documentation\/HeadwireMacKit\/FeatureState\/needsStreaming","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". The features go to the device as the helper’s capabilities, so the device greys out the same controls with the same reasons.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://HeadwireMacKit/documentation/HeadwireMacKit/Onboarding":{"title":"Onboarding","url":"\/documentation\/headwiremackit\/onboarding","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The permission s